epsilon_check.gp --- guard-free re-determination of the unit character eps
curve         E: y^2 = x^3 - 56x, ainvs [0,0,0,-56,0], N = 12544 = 2^8*7^2
backs         the sentence after eq:psiE
PARI/GP       2.17.2
realprecision 3217 decimal digits (the arithmetic below is exact:
              integers, Z/p, and ellap; no real number enters a decision)
prime range   split 5 <= p <= 60000, p != 7

pass 1: residue classes mod 56 determined: 384

CHECK 1  eps depends only on the residue class mod 56
  split primes tested : 3018
  conflicts           : 0
  primes with no unique candidate: 0

CHECK 2  eps = (56/.)_4^{-1}, i.e. CK + m = 0 mod 4 with (56/alpha)_4 = i^m
  primes agreeing     : 3018
  primes disagreeing  : 0

COVERAGE of the 384 classes used by deltaE.gp
  classes covered by the prime range: 384
  classes not reached               : 0

STATUS: eps is consistent at every split prime tested, agrees with the
        closed form (56/.)_4^{-1}, and covers all 384 classes of D_E.
